From e04ad2f12f3adb4c745c3d1288c7613d85d8bf23 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mokuroh54 <mokuroh54@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 5 Aug 2026 11:26:11 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] feat(ui): reveal the full model name on hover, only when it
 is shortened
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Names shorten two ways — CSS truncation and the middleEllipsis fallback —
and neither previously told the user reliably what the full name was:
some surfaces had always-on title attributes, others none. One shared
mechanism now covers both: useTruncationTitle measures CSS clipping at
hover time (scrollWidth vs clientWidth, per hover so resizes need no
observer, sweeping descendants so ModelCard's base+suffix pair works as
one unit) and compares rendered-vs-full for JS shortening; the title
attribute is emitted only when the name is actually shortened.

Applied to ModelCard's title (full display name + import source),
JobCard, HubModelCard (full repo id; namespace peel counts as
shortening), and the DeployPanel picker trigger + items via the
TruncateWithTitle span. No layout, spacing, or truncation changes.
TrainPanel's un-truncated dropdown (defect F) is left for its own fix.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
